24008:
For MY, K_{sp} = s^{2} so s = \sqrt{K_{sp}}
For NY_{3}, K_{sp} = 27s^{4} so s = (\frac{K_{sp}}{27})^{1/4}
Same K_{sp} gives s_{MY} near 7.9 \times 10^{-7} and s_{NY_{3}} near 3.9 \times 10^{-4}
Lower molar solubility of MY which is option A
→ (A)

24011:
Pure water gives [H^{+}] = 10^{-7}
Nernst gives E = -\frac{0.0591}{2}\log\frac{P_{H_{2}}}{[H^{+}]^{2}}
Zero E needs P_{H_{2}} = [H^{+}]^{2} = 10^{-14} atm which is option D
→ (D)

24019:
Rate is proportional to concentration so k = \frac{1}{\Delta t}\ln\frac{r_{1}}{r_{2}}
k = \frac{1}{10}\ln\frac{0.04}{0.03} = \frac{1}{10}\ln\frac{4}{3}
Half life t_{1/2} = \frac{0.693}{k} = \frac{6.93}{\ln(4/3)} \approx 24.1\text{ s}
Value 24.1 s which is option D
→ (D)
